  "notes": "Edit decision list for render_promo.py. Gameplay clip ranges are NATIVE 60 Hz frames (state.csv 'frame'); the FFV1 gameplay.mkv holds every second native frame at 30 fps, so mkv frame = native / 2 and every output frame advances exactly one source frame (normal speed). Title ranges are title.mkv frame indices. Starts must be even, ends exclusive. PACED CUT (2026-10-06): fewer, longer contiguous ranges; captions >=3 s where the ROM stage allows; online card adds an original lead-in graphic before the 120-frame title clip (no footage holds). INTRO-AUDIO REVISION (2026-10-06): a cold-open 'intro' segment is prepended. It is real contiguous EHZ1 footage (native 1200-1684) that ends on exactly the frames the hook shot begins with (native 1660), so the 12-frame 'build' crossfade only changes the surround and the paced edit after it is unchanged (every later segment shifted by the same whole number of frames). 'audio' describes an editorial soundtrack rendered from the Sonic 2 ROM by OpenGGF's SMPS driver; the footage itself was captured silent.",
